    "narrative": "The primary drivers for our offensive output today are **Bryson Stott** (72.63) and **Taylor Ward** (71.19), both of whom benefit from exceptional situational alignment. **Bryson Stott** is our priority play, as the matchup against Chase Dollander features a significant platoon advantage and a slow delivery profile that increases his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given our league's scarcity of speed. Similarly, **Taylor Ward** is positioned to feast in a favorable park against Jacob Lopez, with his efficiency score bolstered by an aggressive platoon-driven projection and an assumed spot at the top of the lineup. Meanwhile, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a staple in our UTIL slot (68.65); despite facing a competent arm in Connor Prielipp, his raw talent floor keeps him ahead of the field in terms of pure offensive contribution.\n\nDecisions in the middle of the roster were dictated by park factors and platoon splits. **Gavin Sheets** (59.46) sneaks into the starting OF rotation over several bench options due to the power potential provided by his platoon edge against Michael McGreevy. The most difficult exclusion today was **Geraldo Perdomo** (47.47); while he possesses the speed we covet, the combination of a tough matchup against Nolan McLean and the inherent risks of a \"Lineup Pending\" status ultimately pushed the optimizer toward more stable, higher-projected bats like **Masyn Winn** and **Lawrence Butler**. The latter, despite facing an elite arm in Kyle Bradish, earns his spot on the strength of a 16% park boost and a massive platoon advantage that offsets the pitcher's quality.\n\nManagement should monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Cal Raleigh** (61.58) and **Will Smith** (43.14). **Will Smith** is our most vulnerable start, as his score is suppressed by a difficult assignment against Chris Sale; if a defensive substitution or rest day is announced, we should be ready to rotate in bench depth. Furthermore, while **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Jung Hoo Lee** are all set to benefit from wind-aided conditions at their venue, any last-minute weather shifts in the Pittsburgh game could necessitate a pivot toward our more insulated assets on the bench, such as **Jonathan Aranda** or **Tyler Freeman**.",
